# Shell scripts must keep LF endings regardless of the checkout platform. A
# CRLF shebang line makes Linux reject the file outright with a "bad
# interpreter" error, which is how scripts/verify-platform.sh broke the first
# time it was copied from a Windows working tree to the platform host.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for the files the containers read: these are bind-mounted into
# Linux images, and some YAML/config parsers keep the trailing \r as part of a
# value.
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
